From c8c383af855dfaac3509ba265b4a0d99c281b3ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:27:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06927/11362] [outer-loop] sk48: L6 SOLVED round 11 (codex,
 first attempt at fresh territory)

Round-11 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L6 on the first attempt. L6
combines two simultaneously-required chain/guide pairs with one
central fixed blocker -- the first level where both pairs start
genuinely unsatisfied. Neither chain can reach its own rack blocks
directly, so the chains cooperate crosswise: each relocates the
other pair's blocks to a boundary. A subtlety: the "nearer" target
position fails due to ordering contamination (a crossing block gets
seen first, corrupting the sequence); the correct target position
avoids this. Boundary release needs one extra retraction after
carrying a block to the edge.

The source agent's own fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed
reached_level=6 independently. The outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=6,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED (frame well-formed, not degenerate).

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: sk48 levels_reproduced 5 -> 6.
reproducible_total_levels 172 -> 173 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
