+  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 6 combines two simultaneously checked chain/guide pairs with one central fixed blocker. The horizontal pair requires 9,9,9 and the vertical pair requires 8,8,8. Neither chain can directly reach its own three rack blocks because the blocker splits its forward lane. The chains must therefore cooperate crosswise: the horizontal chain relocates the vertical pair's three 8 blocks from the blocked x=29 column to the left boundary x=11, and the vertical chain relocates the horizontal pair's three 9 blocks from the blocked y=26 row to the top boundary y=8. Boundary-jammed same-color block components then remain fixed while the matching chain extends through them, permitting all three blocks to be seen in target order. This is the first level where cross-chain block relocation is necessary rather than merely preserving an already-satisfied second pair.",
+  "narrative": "The mandated resolver selected results/outer_loop_codex55_sk48_probe_round9_20260712.json. A fresh env.reset() followed by all 144 resolved labels reproduced frame_level 5 with GameState.NOT_FINISHED exactly. Compact live component dumps mapped L6 as two checked pairs: a horizontal chain at y=26 targeting three 9 blocks and a vertical chain at x=29 targeting three 8 blocks. Both forward lanes are split by the fixed blocker at (29,26). Seven live mapping actions selected the vertical chain, verified two successful forward extensions followed by a blocker-cancelled third extension, and used three ACTION7 undos to restore the initial geometry; energy remained spent. An exact source-grounded search over deep-copied settled game states found a 117-action cooperative solution. The horizontal chain first moved the three 8 blocks left to boundary column x=11, then the vertical chain moved the three 9 blocks upward to boundary row y=8. The vertical chain extended through the pinned boundary-jammed 8 stack, then the horizontal chain extended through the pinned boundary-jammed 9 row. Every live settled-state signature matched the exact predicted transition. The final ACTION4 at full-sequence label 268 advanced frame_level 5 -> 6 with GameState.NOT_FINISHED. A second fresh offline environment replayed the exact 268-label sequence and independently reproduced transitions 0->1 at label 14, 1->2 at 44, 2->3 at 81, 3->4 at 106, 4->5 at 144, and 5->6 at 268.",
+  "gotchas": [
+    "L6 has two genuinely required pairs, not one required pair plus an initially satisfied auxiliary pair: horizontal target 9,9,9 and vertical target 8,8,8 both begin with no active-chain blocks seen.",
